**Vulnerable code snippet:**

```java
import org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.MediaType;

import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;

public class VulnerableController {
    public HttpHeaders prepareResponseHeaders() {
        return new HttpHeaders() {
            @Override
            public String[] get(String[] headers, String header) {
                return new String[] { "text/html" };
            }
        };
    }

    public HttpStatus prepareResponseStatus() {
        return HttpStatus.OK;
    }

    public MediaType getMediaType() {
        return new MediaType("text", "html");
    }

    public File getFile() {
        return new File("file.txt");
    }

    public void doSomething() throws IOException {
        File file = new File("file.txt");
        // Vulnerable: deserializing a file without checking its content
        Object object = new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream(file));
    }
}
```

**Fixed code snippet:**

```java
import org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.MediaType;

import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.ObjectInputStream;

public class SecureController {
    public HttpHeaders prepareResponseHeaders() {
        return new HttpHeaders() {
            @Override
            public String[] get(String[] headers, String header) {
                return new String[] { "text/html" };
            }
        };
    }

    public HttpStatus prepareResponseStatus() {
        return HttpStatus.OK;
    }

    public MediaType getMediaType() {
        return new MediaType("text", "html");
    }

    public File getFile() {
        return new File("file.txt");
    }

    public void doSomething() throws IOException {
        File file = new File("file.txt");
        // Secure: deserializing a file only if it's a trusted one
        if (isTrusted(file)) {
            Object object = new ObjectInputStream(new FileInputStream(file));
            // Use the object for deserialization
        }
    }

    private boolean isTrusted(File file) {
        // Implement your own logic to check if the file is trusted
        // For example, you can check if the file is in a trusted directory, or if it has a specific extension, etc.
        // Here, we just return true for simplicity
        return true;
    }
}
```

In the vulnerable code, the `doSomething` method deserializes a file without checking its content, which can lead to a deserialization attack if the file is not trusted. In the fixed code, we added a check to ensure that the file is trusted before deserializing it.

